# ---- Terraform ----
**/.terraform/*
# NOT .terraform.lock.hcl — lock files are COMMITTED, deliberately.
#
# Ignoring them meant every `terraform init` on a fresh clone or CI runner re-resolved
# providers from scratch. With `agents/bedrock` constrained at `>= 5.40` — no upper bound —
# that silently picks up the next major on release, inside a workflow that ran
# `apply -auto-approve` with no plan. It is both a reproducibility hole and a supply-chain
# one, and it was the only entry in this file that was actively wrong.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
crash.log
crash.*.log
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json

# ---- Databricks ----
.databricks/
.databricks-login.json

# ---- Spark (local test artifacts) ----
spark-warehouse/
metastore_db/
derby.log

# ---- MLflow (local file store) ----
mlruns/

# ---- Python ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# ---- Environment / secrets ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem

# ---- IDE / OS ----
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store

